Firefighters are continuing to battle huge forest fires across France and Spain on Monday, as authorities warned that another heatwave could bring temperatures of up to 40C to the already scorched wine-growing region around Bordeaux.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b3a2b2-8983-11f1-8ce6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3987H6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b3a2b2-8983-11f1-8ce6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3987H6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08ea9bda-8983-11f1-b9cc-e5a49bdb74b3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 06:36:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b3a2b2-8983-11f1-8ce6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3987H6.jpg">AFP - ROMAIN PERROCHEAU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>No snakes in church and don't eat the frogs: the weird world of US animal laws</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260726-no-snakes-in-church-and-don-t-eat-the-frogs-the-weird-world-of-us-animal-laws</link><description>
